🚨➡️💡 **SUGGESTION (follow-up hardening — the round-1 footgun's last trace)**

The two projects fetches and the two models fetches speak **different `apiBase` conventions**, and only half of it is documented:

- `fetchCodeMieModels` / `fetchCodeMieModelsWithJwt` — [apiBase] is `<org>/code-assistant-api/v1` (documented; they append `/llm_models`).
- `fetchCodeMieProjects` / `fetchCodeMieProjectsWithJwt` — [apiBase] is `<org>/code-assistant-api` (they append `/v1/user` themselves) — **only implicit** in the "from `<apiBase>/v1/user`" wording.

This asymmetry is exactly what produced round 1's blocking double-`/v1` (`…/code-assistant-api/v1/v1/user`). The r2 fix (call-site convention + exact-path mock matchers) is correct and the mocks now catch a regression loudly — but a future caller reading only `fetchCodeMieProjectsWithJwt`'s one-line doc has no guard against repeating the mistake.

Suggest one doc line on both projects fetches, matching the models fetches' style:

```dart
/// Fetches the user's accessible projects from `<apiBase>/v1/user`.
/// [apiBase] is `<org>/code-assistant-api` — WITHOUT the `/v1` segment
/// (unlike [fetchCodeMieModels], which takes the `/v1` base); this call
/// appends `/v1/user` itself.
```

Docs-only, no behavior change — fine to fold into a follow-up.

